      "summaries": {
        "en": "12-factor-agents is a set of principles for building production-grade LLM-powered applications, inspired by the 12-factor app methodology. It addresses common pitfalls like context window mismanagement and lack of observability by advocating for explicit state, modular tooling, and robust logging. Developers can apply these patterns to design agents that are scalable, maintainable, and reliable in real-world deployments, making it easier to move from prototype to production.",
        "zh": "12-factor-agents 是一套构建生产级 LLM 应用的原则，借鉴了 12-factor 应用方法论。它针对上下文窗口管理不当、缺乏可观测性等常见问题，提出显式状态管理、模块化工具设计和健壮日志记录等核心实践。开发者可遵循这些模式，设计出可扩展、易维护且可靠的智能体系统，从而顺利从原型过渡到生产环境。该框架强调工程化思维，帮助团队避免常见陷阱，提升 LLM 应用的稳定性和可调试性。",
        "es": "12-factor-agents is a set of principles for building production-grade LLM-powered applications, inspired by the 12-factor app methodology. It addresses common pitfalls like context window mismanagement and lack of observability by advocating for explicit state, modular tooling, and robust logging. Developers can apply these patterns to design agents that are scalable, maintainable, and reliable in real-world deployments, making it easier to move from prototype to production.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "12-factor-agents stands out for 12-factor, 12-factor-agents, and agents in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "12-factor-agents is a set of principles for building production-grade LLM-powered applications, inspired by the 12-factor app methodology. It addresses common pitfalls like context window mismanagement and lack of observability by advocating for explicit state, modular tooling, and robust logging. Developers can apply these patterns to design agents that are scalable, maintainable, and reliable in real-world deployments, making it easier to move from prototype to production.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/humanlayer/12-factor-agents for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
